# The salt must never be published. Combined with the deposit it lets an attacker
# compute the rank of a guessed (line, column, mutator, replacement) tuple and test
# it against the published ordering, which restores the verification oracle the
# opaque labels exist to remove. See publicSalt() in analyze.ts.
.public-salt

# Raw Stryker reports embed the full source of every mutated file.
reports/
*.stryker.json

# Tooling and editor artefacts
.claude/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log
